-- **`masks irqs` in a Linux kernel module -- the C realises the masking**
-- (server lane, TODO section 0e K3; OFFEN O19's C half for the module target).
--
-- WHAT THIS PROBE ANSWERS. `lock … masks irqs` is a promise about the
-- environment: while the lock is held, no interrupt handler runs on this core.
-- Until 2026-09-28 the emitted C kept that promise on bare metal only
-- (`METALL_SPERRE_MASKIERT`, Opus agent J), and a `module` unit with ONE lock
-- did not link at all -- `ERROR: modpost: "TAKT_nimm" … undefined!`. Now
-- `laufzeit/kmodul/sperre.h` defines the primitives, and a MASKED lock becomes
-- `raw_spin_lock_irqsave`.
--
-- HOW IT IS MEASURED, and why it is a measurement and not an absence of bad
-- news. The program runs 64 rounds, each of which holds `TAKT` across a full
-- traversal of a 4096-slot table -- a critical section long enough that a timer
-- firing every 50 us would land inside it many times over. Beside it the
-- program's OWN C arms a kernel timer in HARDIRQ mode whose body calls `tick`
-- below, which takes the same lock. The timer body reads the runtime's
-- `gabbro_halter_TAKT` (the core that holds the lock, or -1) BEFORE it takes
-- the lock, and counts how often it landed on a core that was holding.
--
--   masked   ticks > 0 and landed = 0 -- interrupts arrive, never inside
--   plain    the handler lands inside and then waits for the core it
--            interrupted: the same-core deadlock `H102` refuses
--            (`beispiele/gift/460`), and the harness's poison run hangs
--
-- `ticks > 0` is the half that makes the other half mean anything: a run in
-- which the timer never fired would report `landed=0` and have measured
-- nothing. The harness checks both.
--
-- **Every call into the kernel is the PROGRAM's** (Simon, 2026-09-27). This
-- unit names three foreign functions with their shape, effects, cost and the
-- assumption their bodies keep; the bodies are the program's own C
-- (`messung/proben/kmodul/takt.c`), which is where `hrtimer` and `pr_info`
-- stand. Nothing about Linux is in this file.
--
-- **What this probe does NOT claim.** A Linux timer callback is not an
-- `entry … vector V via idt`: the kernel calls it, no vector is the program's,
-- and `H102` -- which reads exactly that word -- stays silent here. So the
-- masking is REALISED for the module target and it is not yet CHECKED for it
-- (OFFEN O19, the module row).
module treiber::takt {

assume kmod_takt_vertrag
    "The module's own `gabbro_kmod_takt_*` bodies keep the x86_64 SysV convention and return: `_melde` writes its two words to the kernel log, `_an` arms a hardirq timer whose body calls `tick`, `_aus` cancels it and reports the two counters."
    falsifier sonde_kmod_takt;

-- The kernel API, declared here and nowhere else.
extern fn gabbro_kmod_takt_melde(schluessel : u32, wert : u64) effects { pure } costs <= 64 ops;
extern fn gabbro_kmod_takt_an() effects { pure } costs <= 512 ops;
extern fn gabbro_kmod_takt_aus() effects { pure } costs <= 512 ops;

pub table Takte count 4096 {
    slot { stand : u64, }
}

table Runden count 64 {
    slot { getan : u64, }
}

-- **The one word this probe is about.** Without `masks irqs` the same file is
-- the deadlock: `tick` below enters on the core that holds `TAKT`.
pub lock TAKT protects { Takte } rank 0 held <= 20000 ops masks irqs;

-- **The short critical section, entered by the hardware side.** `pub`, because
-- the program's own C calls it and that C is a translation unit of its own --
-- the emitted unit is `#include`d by the driver, so a `static` body would not
-- be nameable from there.
pub fn tick()
    effects { reads Takte, reads Takte.slots, writes Takte.slots, locks TAKT }
    costs   <= 64 ops
{
    locks TAKT {
        Takte.slots[0].stand = 1;
    }
}

-- **The long critical section, entered by the thread side.** One pass over the
-- whole table under the lock: the window a timer would land in.
fn runde()
    effects { reads Takte, reads Takte.slots, writes Takte.slots, locks TAKT }
    costs   <= 20000 ops
{
    locks TAKT {
        traverse i over slots of Takte by unvisited {
            Takte.slots[i].stand = 1;
        }
    }
}

-- Load: arm the timer, run the rounds, cancel the timer and report.
impl fn laden() -> u32
    effects { reads Takte, reads Takte.slots, writes Takte.slots,
              reads Runden, reads Runden.slots, writes Runden.slots, locks TAKT }
    costs   <= 2000000 ops
{
    gabbro_kmod_takt_melde(1, 0);
    gabbro_kmod_takt_an();
    traverse r over slots of Runden by unvisited {
        -- The round is marked, and that is not decoration: a table used only as
        -- a traversal DOMAIN has storage nothing touches, and `clang` refuses
        -- the emitted `static Runden Runden_speicher` as
        -- `-Wunneeded-internal-declaration` (measured by `pruefe-emission.sh`
        -- stage 9's clang half, 2026-09-28).
        Runden.slots[r].getan = 1;
        runde();
    }
    gabbro_kmod_takt_aus();
    return 0;
}

-- Unload: one line. The timer is already cancelled; the table is static.
impl fn entladen() -> u32 effects { pure } costs <= 64 ops {
    gabbro_kmod_takt_melde(9, 0);
    return 0;
}

}
